# Spec-driven development

Behavior and API contracts live in `.specify/specs/` (constitution: `.specify/memory/constitution.md`).

- Before changing user-visible behavior, cookies, tokens, storage, routes, or HTTP APIs, read the matching spec. Auth is `.specify/specs/001-authentication/` — including `contracts/auth.md` and `gaps.md`.
- If code and spec disagree, change the spec first or change the code to match. Do not add unspecified cookies, `localStorage` tokens, or headers.
- The UI never writes auth cookies. `credentials: 'include'` does not create them. Login `Set-Cookie` is backend-only (`refresh_token`).
- New features: copy `.specify/templates/` into `.specify/specs/NNN-name/`, then implement tasks only.
- Do not treat `FEATURES.md` or `PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md` as the contract; they index `.specify/specs/`.
- Do not create a second `specs/` folder at the repo root.
